reccmp master: Import structs with flexible array members (FAM)

Upstream's `_overwrite_struct` places every PDB field with
`replaceAtOffset`.  C flexible array members (`Type name[];`) are encoded
in the PDB as a zero-length `LF_ARRAY` whose offset equals the struct's
fixed size (i.e. just past the last fixed field).  For such a component
`Structure.getComponentAt(offset)` returns `None` (nothing starts at
`offset == length`), so the importer's
`assert existing_type is not None` raises `AssertionError`, which the
broad `except` surfaces as `StructModificationError`.  Even without the
assertion, `replaceAtOffset` would throw
`IllegalArgumentException: Offset N is beyond end of structure`.

This affects any type with a trailing `name[]`, e.g. Toy Story 2's
`Toy2::Levels::RecordData` (`data[]`), `Toy2::Levels::ObjectList`
(`entries[]`), `Nu3D::Font` (`glyphs[]`), and
`Renderer::...TileSheet` (`tiles[]`).  Because types are imported lazily
on demand, one missing FAM type fans out to many logged failures.

This patch detects zero-length array components and appends them via
`Structure.add(type, 0, name, comment)` instead of `replaceAtOffset`.
Ghidra treats a zero-length trailing component as a flexible array, and
the struct's reported size stays equal to the PDB size (so the existing
size assertions still hold).  The component must already be the last
entry (components are sorted by offset and a FAM sits at `offset ==
class_size`); a warning is logged if that invariant is violated.

Generated against reccmp master (commit 21416ad1) with the
reccmp-union-write patch already applied.
Apply from the reccmp submodule root with `patch -p1`.

diff --git a/reccmp/ghidra/importer/type_importer.py b/reccmp/ghidra/importer/type_importer.py
index e72640e1..3a562277 100644
--- a/reccmp/ghidra/importer/type_importer.py
+++ b/reccmp/ghidra/importer/type_importer.py
@@ -474,6 +474,37 @@ def _overwrite_struct(
             logger.debug("Adding component %s to class: %s", component, sanitized_name)
 
             try:
+                # Flexible array members (C trailing `Type name[];`) are encoded
+                # in the PDB as a zero-length LF_ARRAY whose offset equals the
+                # struct's fixed size (i.e. just past the last fixed field).
+                # Ghidra cannot place such a component with replaceAtOffset --
+                # getComponentAt(offset) returns None and replaceAtOffset raises
+                # "Offset N is beyond end of structure" -- so append it as a
+                # zero-length trailing component, which Ghidra treats as a
+                # flexible array without changing the struct's reported size.
+                if (
+                    isinstance(component.type, ArrayDataType)
+                    and component.type.getNumElements() == 0
+                ):
+                    expected_offset = new_ghidra_struct.getLength()
+                    if offset != expected_offset:
+                        logger.warning(
+                            "Flexible array member %s at offset %d of %s is not at "
+                            "the end of the struct (expected %d); placing it at %d",
+                            component.name,
+                            offset,
+                            sanitized_name,
+                            expected_offset,
+                            expected_offset,
+                        )
+                    new_ghidra_struct.add(
+                        component.type,
+                        0,  # zero-length: do not grow the struct
+                        component.name,
+                        cast(str, None),  # comment
+                    )
+                    continue
+
